          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "gracilis is a native Latin adjective; Lewis & Short compares an old Latin word for \"slender\", but the origin is not settled. English gracile comes from it; grace does not."
            }
          ]
        },
